+# Delivery Plan
+
+## Timeline
+
+| Milestone | Start | End |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| kickoff | 2026-08-24 | 2026-08-26 |
+| requirements | 2026-08-27 | 2026-09-07 |
+| architecture | 2026-09-08 | 2026-09-14 |
+| build-core | 2026-09-15 | 2026-10-01 |
+| build-integrations | 2026-10-02 | 2026-10-15 |
+| hardening | 2026-10-16 | 2026-10-23 |
+| acceptance | 2026-10-26 | 2026-10-29 |
+| launch | 2026-10-30 | 2026-11-02 |
+
+## Countdown
+
+| Business days until kickoff | 5 |
+| --- | --- |
+| Total business days | 48 |
+
+## Notes
+
+The plan is strictly sequential: eight milestones run back-to-back with no
+gaps, starting Monday 2026-08-24 and finishing Monday 2026-11-02 — 48
+business days spanning roughly ten calendar weeks.
+
+The shape is front-loaded with definition and back-loaded with assurance:
+kickoff, requirements, and architecture take the first three and a half
+weeks, then the two build phases consume 21 of the 48 business days (build-
+core alone is the longest milestone at 12), and hardening, acceptance, and
+launch close out the final four weeks.
+
+Things worth calling out:
+
+- All three company holidays (2026-08-31, 2026-09-25, 2026-10-12) fall
+  inside the delivery window. Each one pushes a milestone's end date out —
+  requirements stretches across the first, build-core across the second,
+  and build-integrations across the third — so those milestones span more
+  calendar time than their durations suggest.
+- Launch starts Friday 2026-10-30 and straddles a weekend, ending Monday
+  2026-11-02. If a same-week launch matters, pulling launch forward one
+  business day requires trimming a day from acceptance.
+- The long build-core stretch has no intermediate checkpoint; if it slips,
+  everything after it slides day-for-day.
